'''Justiciar armour''' is a set of armour requiring 75 [[Defence]] to equip. The armour belonged to the [[Saradomin]]ist [[Justiciar]]s, an elite group of warriors active during the God Wars and most notably in the defence of Hallowvale against the vampyre forces of Lord Drakan. After their defeat, their armour was claimed as trophies by the vampyres and came into the possession of Verzik Vitur.{{CiteNews|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=news/the-theatre-of-blood?oldschool=1|title=The Theatre of Blood|newsdate=7 June 2018|quote=The Justiciars were elite warriors in Saradomin's army during the God Wars. Unlike the rest of his forces, the Justiciars operated alone, often working as assassins and saboteurs. Selected from a variety of races, they were all chosen by Saradomin himself who granted them great power. When the vampyres invaded Hallowvale, some of the last remaining Justiciars fell in battle. The Justiciar armour found in Lady Verzik's vault was taken from one of these fallen warriors.}} The set can only be obtained as rare drops from the [[Theatre of Blood]]. 

It is the best armour in ''Old School RuneScape'' to provide [[Melee]] and [[Ranged]] defence bonuses, far surpassing [[Torag the Corrupted's equipment|Torag's armour]] as well as having a damage-reducing [[passive effect|set effect]]. The justiciar armour also provides a significant amount of [[Prayer]] bonus. However, it penalises both magic and ranged attack bonuses more than any other melee armour and provides a negative magic defence, and it also does not provide any strength bonus.

The armour can be stored in the [[armour case]] of a [[player-owned house]] [[costume room]]. The set pieces count as [[Saradomin]]ist items in both the [[God Wars Dungeon|normal]] and [[Wilderness God Wars Dungeon]]s.

==Set effect==
When the full set of Justiciar armour is equipped, the player gains a [[passive effect|set effect]] that reduces all combat damage outside of [[Player killing|PvP]] and typeless damage. The exact formula for the amount of damage reduced is <math>\frac{bonus}{3000}</math>, where bonus is the player's defence bonus for that particular style. If the enemy was using a crush-based attack and the player has a crush defence bonus of +450, then 15% of the damage (450/3,000) is reduced. The set effect always reduces incoming damage by a minimum of 1; negative defence bonuses will not increase damage taken. The set effect stacks additively with the [[elysian spirit shield]]'s passive effect as well.

