==Trivia==
*Design A from the design poll can be seen within [[Verzik Vitur]]'s throne room within the [[Theatre of Blood]].
*The Justiciar design resembles the helms of the Seven Priestly Warriors, as seen in the [[Varrock Museum#/media/File:Varrock Museum display 23.png|Varrock museum]]. However, the Seven Priestly Warriors fought during the year 1200 of the Fourth Age, and based on the account of [[the turncloak]], it is doubtful that the Justiciar order survived the God Wars.
*Based on the statues found in the [[Hallowed Sepulchre]], the Justiciar set of armour obtainable from the Theatre of Blood is most similar in appearance to the armour of the Justiciar of the Wolf, [[Phosani]]. However, her armour (after her change in allegiance to Zamorak) is the [[Inquisitor's armour]] set,{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/the-nightmare-of-ashihama?oldschool=1|title=The Nightmare of Ashihama|newsdate=6 February 2020|quote=The Inquisitor's Armour once belonged to The Inquisitor. She crafted it from her old Justiciar garb, altering it to better reflect her newfound ferocity.}} which suggests the armour Verzik has was either from some other Justiciar or a spare set.
* According to some dialogue with [[Vanescula Drakan]] during [[Sins of the Father]], it is revealed that Lady Verzik and Ranis Drakan tortured one of [[Queen Efaritay]]'s Justiciars for information that would lead to a successful kidnapping of [[King Ascertes]].{{CiteNPC|npc=Vanescula Drakan|quote=I'd give [Verzik] the credit over Ranis. The two of them shared a love for playing with their food rather than eating it. They hatched all kinds of schemes together. During the war, they managed to capture a justiciar, one of Efaritay's most elite warriors. They tortured him for days, until he gave them what they needed.|loc=Sins of the Father}} After getting the information they needed, they killed the Justiciar, and it is likely that Lady Verzik kept the armour as a trophy, which could offer a canon explanation as to how she acquired the two sets of Justiciar armour present in her treasure room. Since the Design A armour described and pictured above is not depicted on any of the statues of the four known Justiciars, it is possible that more than four Justiciars exist or once existed.

